{"call_id":"call_VoftiZpH9iB0tZPMrLW4tmTl","process_id":"69156","turn_id":"019ca6e9-fc8e-7c12-ba89-c6d0edbcd1d6","command":["/usr/bin/bash","-lc","kspec inbox list | head -n 80"],"cwd":"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"kspec inbox list"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","stdout":"Inbox (122 items):\n\n  01KFH76C (1/21/2026 by @claude) [design, spec-model, meta]\n    Cross-feature requirement pattern: How to express that core features (search, validate, export) must support all entity types. When new entity type added, should automatically imply tasks for core features. Options: (1) applies_to field on feature specs, (2) trait on entity types like @trait-searchable, (3) validation warning for missing coverage, (4) parent spec that entity types must satisfy. Surfaced when realizing search doesn't cover inbox.\n\n  01KFHJNZ (1/21/2026 by @claude) [dx, tooling, reflection]\n    Reverse spec lookup - kspec which <file> or kspec which <file:line> to find specs/ACs that reference or are implemented by a given code path. Useful for bug fixes to quickly discover what specs need updating. Could scan for // AC: annotations and spec_ref links. Instructive, helps find already-instrumented code.\n\n  01KFPDCY (1/23/2026 by @claude) [ci, testing, dx]\n    Add cross-platform CI matrix testing - run core functionality tests on Windows, macOS, and Linux. Would catch issues like Unix-specific commands (which, cp -r) before they reach PR review. Consider: matrix strategy in GitHub Actions, platform-specific test skips where needed, focus on CLI commands and daemon lifecycle.\n\n  01KFQ517 (1/23/2026 by @claude) [e2e, testing, reflection]\n    E2E tests: Use isolated port range (not 3456) + cross-platform cleanup. Current approach conflicts with existing daemons. Should use high ephemeral port range and improve cleanup mechanism.\n\n  01KFYAHF (1/26/2026 by @claude) [e2e, dx]\n    E2E test dev mode - configure Playwright to work with vite dev server instead of requiring full build for faster test iteration (12+ seconds to 1-2 seconds)\n\n  01KGG6GY (3 weeks ago by @claude)\n    Improve derive granularity: Research suggests specs with 4+ ACs are candidates for splitting. Potential enhancements: (1) --by-ac flag to create tasks per AC group, (2) --max-acs N to auto-group, (3) implementation_phases field in specs, (4) derive templates for common patterns (cli-command, api-endpoint), (5) complexity warnings when specs are too large. See session research on task decomposition patterns from Linear, Atlassian, BDD/Example Mapping, and AI coding assistants.\n\n  01KGGEMM (3 weeks ago by @claude) [daemon, dx, deferred]\n    Daemon debugging improvements: (1) Add --log-file or --verbose to 'kspec serve start', (2) Log resolved web UI path on startup, (3) Capture and show stderr when daemon fails to start within timeout. Consolidated from @01KFQ586, @01KFQ595, @01KFPH3D.\n\n  01KGGF4Y (3 weeks ago by @claude) [feature, config, dx, deferred]\n    Project config file (kspec.config.yaml or .kspecrc): Configure shadow remote URL (enable separate repo for specs), feature toggles, default values (author, priority), validation strictness. Enables multi-repo projects sharing specs and tailoring kspec to project needs. Consolidated from @01KFGVVJ, @01KFGVVN.\n\n  01KGGFB2 (3 weeks ago by @claude) [cli, testing, dx]\n    AC test coverage analysis: 'kspec coverage @spec-ref' command to scan codebase for '// AC: @spec ac-N' annotations and report which ACs have test coverage vs gaps. Soft check for review, not blocking. Consolidated from @01KFHJNR, @01KFP9A6.\n\n  01KGGG0K (3 weeks ago by @claude) [shadow, dx, cli]\n    Shadow sync improvements: (1) Auto-resolve using rebase/merge-driver for cleaner sync, (2) Make sync warnings visible in CLI output (currently silent unless KSPEC_DEBUG=1), (3) Auto-detect common issues with suggested fixes. Consolidated from @01KFTDA7, @01KFHZR4.\n\n  01KGGKNX (3 weeks ago by @claude) [cli, design, dx]\n    CLI array field flag patterns: (1) Generic --clear <field> or --<field> [] for clearing arrays, (2) --add-<field> vs multiple flags for append semantics. Design unified approach for depends-on, tags, blocked-by, etc. Consolidated from @01KFGRV6, @01KFR0KN.\n\n  01KGGP9F (3 weeks ago by @claude) [cli, inbox, dx]\n    Inbox CLI improvements: (1) Add filtering to list: --before/--after <date>, --author <name> (--tag exists), (2) Add merge command: 'kspec inbox merge @source @target' for consolidating duplicates, (3) Add --priority and --automation flags to promote command. Consolidated from @01KG95JP, @01KG95JQ, @01KG95JS.\n\n  01KGGPJ6 (3 weeks ago by @claude) [workflow, cli, dx]\n    Workflow CLI improvements: (1) 'workflow show' should infer active run like 'workflow next', (2) Warn when --input flags passed but step has no inputs defined, (3) Improve 'workflow show' output format with vertical display, status indicators, indented notes. Consolidated from @01KFKSF6, @01KFKSGC, @01KFKTNR.\n\n  01KGGPSR (3 weeks ago by @claude) [cli, validation, ux]\n    Spec item slug/addressing improvements: (1) Warn/error on slug collision when creating items, (2) Make nested requirements addressable by slug (currently kspec item ac add @slug fails for items under requirements:). Consolidated from @01KGDCRG, @01KGDCRJ.\n\n  01KGGTT3 (3 weeks ago by @claude) [cli, batch, dx]\n    Expand @trait-multi-ref-batch to remaining commands: trait add/remove, task set --automation, inbox delete, task note. Enables batch operations like 'kspec task note @ref1 @ref2 @ref3 \"shared content\"'. Consolidated from @01KG71J2, @01KG95JM, @01KFVXBM.\n\n  01KGKVK9 (3 weeks ago by @claude) [cli, reflection]\n    Add --spec-ref filter to kspec task list command to filter tasks by linked spec item\n\n  01KGQY6Q (3 weeks ago by @claude) [workflow, cli, dx, deferred]\n    Workflow lifecycle CLI design (from mining run 01KFS6MJ): kspec workflow complete @run-ref (mark run completed, archive), kspec workflow cancel @run-ref (cancel abandoned run), kspec workflow cleanup --older-than Nd (auto-cancel stale runs). Extends existing @01KFPH39 auto-cleanup with concrete subcommand design.\n\n  01KGVK8R (3 weeks ago by @claude) [cli, dx, reflection]\n    Item list --module flag and tree view: kspec item list --module cli to scope output to a specific module. kspec item tree @module for hierarchical view (features -> requirements). Currently 50+ items display flat, making it hard to find the right parent for new specs. Friction: during automation triage had to grep YAML files to find parent specs.\n\n  01KGWG99 (3 weeks ago by @claude) [reflection, sessions, schema]\n    Define typed event data schemas per EventType — session.start, session.update (with tool_call/sessionUpdate variants), session.end, prompt.sent, tool.call, tool.result, note. Current z.unknown() data field makes it impossible to reliably query events without reverse-engineering from real JSONL files.\n\n  01KGWQ2T (3 weeks ago by @claude) [deferred]\n    Session log compaction: at end of each ralph loop, replace raw events.jsonl with a compiled stats file (event counts by type, tool usage frequency, duration, task transitions, error summary). Keep session folders and context snapshots intact but prune the raw log. This gives trend analysis capability without unbounded log growth. Could be a kspec session compact command or automatic post-loop step.\n\n  01KGWZR7 (3 weeks ago by @claude) [reflection, meta, architecture]\n    Active context from meta: use the meta database (observations, conventions, patterns) as a dynamic context source that automatically surfaces relevant entries based on current activity. E.g. when reviewing plan-import code, auto-surface friction observations tagged with plan-import. When doing code review, pull in resolved friction patterns as review priors. Replaces manual markdown maintenance (AGENTS.md, skill docs) with structured data that stays current as observations accumulate. Could use conventions or a new meta item type for durable patterns distinct from one-off observations.\n\n  01KH20S1 (2 weeks ago by @claude) [code-hygiene, dx]\n    Centralize daemon port default (3456) — currently hardcoded in 6 places: src/schema/spec.ts, src/cli/index.ts, src/cli/commands/serve.ts, packages/daemon/src/index.ts, packages/web-ui/src/lib/constants.ts, packages/web-ui/tests/fixtures/test-base.ts. Extract to a shared constant to prevent drift.\n\n  01KHA982 (2 weeks ago by @claude)\n    Formalize CLI usage analysis as a repeatable workflow. Tools exist in .claude-research/tools/ (parse-ralph-logs.mjs, parse-claude-logs.mjs, compile-data.mjs) plus interactive HTML report. Consider: kspec skill, CLI command, or standalone workflow. Re-run after implementing the 6 CLI agent-UX improvements to measure impact.\n\n  01KHCYW7 (2 weeks ago by @claude) [cli, dx, reflection]\n    Add repeated-flag support to --status filter (ac-repeated-flag gap from PR #354). Commander.js .option() needs a collect function to accumulate repeated --status flags into an array. Currently only comma-separated works. Small fix: change .option('-s, --status <status>') to use Commander's variadic/collect pattern, then feed array into parseMultiStatus().\n\n  01KHF37M (2 weeks ago by @claude)\n    Shadow branch diff/changelog — since .kspec/ is git-tracked, we could show changes to stored artifacts (workflows, tasks, specs, inbox) over time. Something like kspec history @ref or kspec diff --since '1 week ago' that leverages the git history on kspec-meta branch. Could show task state transitions, spec evolution, workflow modifications, etc.\n\n  01KHFCDS (2 weeks ago by @claude)\n    Version pinning: all projects use whatever global kspec version is installed. No lock file or constraint resolution. Consider adding version constraints to kynetic.yaml manifest.\n\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"Inbox (122 items):\n\n  01KFH76C (1/21/2026 by @claude) [design, spec-model, meta]\n    Cross-feature requirement pattern: How to express that core features (search, validate, export) must support all entity types. When new entity type added, should automatically imply tasks for core features. Options: (1) applies_to field on feature specs, (2) trait on entity types like @trait-searchable, (3) validation warning for missing coverage, (4) parent spec that entity types must satisfy. Surfaced when realizing search doesn't cover inbox.\n\n  01KFHJNZ (1/21/2026 by @claude) [dx, tooling, reflection]\n    Reverse spec lookup - kspec which <file> or kspec which <file:line> to find specs/ACs that reference or are implemented by a given code path. Useful for bug fixes to quickly discover what specs need updating. Could scan for // AC: annotations and spec_ref links. Instructive, helps find already-instrumented code.\n\n  01KFPDCY (1/23/2026 by @claude) [ci, testing, dx]\n    Add cross-platform CI matrix testing - run core functionality tests on Windows, macOS, and Linux. Would catch issues like Unix-specific commands (which, cp -r) before they reach PR review. Consider: matrix strategy in GitHub Actions, platform-specific test skips where needed, focus on CLI commands and daemon lifecycle.\n\n  01KFQ517 (1/23/2026 by @claude) [e2e, testing, reflection]\n    E2E tests: Use isolated port range (not 3456) + cross-platform cleanup. Current approach conflicts with existing daemons. Should use high ephemeral port range and improve cleanup mechanism.\n\n  01KFYAHF (1/26/2026 by @claude) [e2e, dx]\n    E2E test dev mode - configure Playwright to work with vite dev server instead of requiring full build for faster test iteration (12+ seconds to 1-2 seconds)\n\n  01KGG6GY (3 weeks ago by @claude)\n    Improve derive granularity: Research suggests specs with 4+ ACs are candidates for splitting. Potential enhancements: (1) --by-ac flag to create tasks per AC group, (2) --max-acs N to auto-group, (3) implementation_phases field in specs, (4) derive templates for common