ve run like 'workflow next', (2) Warn when --input flags passed but step has no inputs defined, (3) Improve 'workflow show' output format with vertical display, status indicators, indented notes. Consolidated from @01KFKSF6, @01KFKSGC, @01KFKTNR.\n\n  01KGGPSR (3 weeks ago by @claude) [cli, validation, ux]\n    Spec item slug/addressing improvements: (1) Warn/error on slug collision when creating items, (2) Make nested requirements addressable by slug (currently kspec item ac add @slug fails for items under requirements:). Consolidated from @01KGDCRG, @01KGDCRJ.\n\n  01KGGTT3 (3 weeks ago by @claude) [cli, batch, dx]\n    Expand @trait-multi-ref-batch to remaining commands: trait add/remove, task set --automation, inbox delete, task note. Enables batch operations like 'kspec task note @ref1 @ref2 @ref3 \"shared content\"'. Consolidated from @01KG71J2, @01KG95JM, @01KFVXBM.\n\n  01KGKVK9 (3 weeks ago by @claude) [cli, reflection]\n    Add --spec-ref filter to kspec task list command to filter tasks by linked spec item\n\n  01KGQY6Q (3 weeks ago by @claude) [workflow, cli, dx, deferred]\n    Workflow lifecycle CLI design (from mining run 01KFS6MJ): kspec workflow complete @run-ref (mark run completed, archive), kspec workflow cancel @run-ref (cancel abandoned run), kspec workflow cleanup --older-than Nd (auto-cancel stale runs). Extends existing @01KFPH39 auto-cleanup with concrete subcommand design.\n\n  01KGVK8R (3 weeks ago by @claude) [cli, dx, reflection]\n    Item list --module flag and tree view: kspec item list --module cli to scope output to a specific module. kspec item tree @module for hierarchical view (features -> requirements). Currently 50+ items display flat, making it hard to find the right parent for new specs. Friction: during automation triage had to grep YAML files to find parent specs.\n\n  01KGWG99 (3 weeks ago by @claude) [reflection, sessions, schema]\n    Define typed event data schemas per EventType — session.start, session.update (with tool_call/sessionUpdate variants), session.end, prompt.sent, tool.call, tool.result, note. Current z.unknown() data field makes it impossible to reliably query events without reverse-engineering from real JSONL files.\n\n  01KGWQ2T (3 weeks ago by @claude) [deferred]\n    Session log compaction: at end of each ralph loop, replace raw events.jsonl with a compiled stats file (event counts by type, tool usage frequency, duration, task transitions, error summary). Keep session folders and context snapshots intact but prune the raw log. This gives trend analysis capability without unbounded log growth. Could be a kspec session compact command or automatic post-loop step.\n\n  01KGWZR7 (3 weeks ago by @claude) [reflection, meta, architecture]\n    Active context from meta: use the meta database (observations, conventions, patterns) as a dynamic context source that automatically surfaces relevant entries based on current activity. E.g. when reviewing plan-import code, auto-surface friction observations tagged with plan-import. When doing code review, pull in resolved friction patterns as review priors. Replaces manual markdown maintenance (AGENTS.md, skill docs) with structured data that stays current as observations accumulate. Could use conventions or a new meta item type for durable patterns distinct from one-off observations.\n\n  01KH20S1 (2 weeks ago by @claude) [code-hygiene, dx]\n    Centralize daemon port default (3456) — currently hardcoded in 6 places: src/schema/spec.ts, src/cli/index.ts, src/cli/commands/serve.ts, packages/daemon/src/index.ts, packages/web-ui/src/lib/constants.ts, packages/web-ui/tests/fixtures/test-base.ts. Extract to a shared constant to prevent drift.\n\n  01KHA982 (2 weeks ago by @claude)\n    Formalize CLI usage analysis as a repeatable workflow. Tools exist in .claude-research/tools/ (parse-ralph-logs.mjs, parse-claude-logs.mjs, compile-data.mjs) plus interactive HTML report. Consider: kspec skill, CLI command, or standalone workflow. Re-run after implementing the 6 CLI agent-UX improvements to measure impact.\n\n  01KHCYW7 (2 weeks ago by @claude) [cli, dx, reflection]\n    Add repeated-flag support to --status filter (ac-repeated-flag gap from PR #354). Commander.js .option() needs a collect function to accumulate repeated --status flags into an array. Currently only comma-separated works. Small fix: change .option('-s, --status <status>') to use Commander's variadic/collect pattern, then feed array into parseMultiStatus().\n\n  01KHF37M (2 weeks ago by @claude)\n    Shadow branch diff/changelog — since .kspec/ is git-tracked, we could show changes to stored artifacts (workflows, tasks, specs, inbox) over time. Something like kspec history @ref or kspec diff --since '1 week ago' that leverages the git history on kspec-meta branch. Could show task state transitions, spec evolution, workflow modifications, etc.\n\n  01KHFCDS (2 weeks ago by @claude)\n    Version pinning: all projects use whatever global kspec version is installed. No lock file or constraint resolution. Consider adding version constraints to kynetic.yaml manifest.\n\n","status":"completed"}